<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged, grain merchandisers in the U.S. High Plains said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dealers said farmer selling of wheat was slow Monday in response to the slide in KCBT wheat futures prices.</p>
<p>The weekly state crop reports released Monday afternoon rated that more than 80 percent of the wheat in Kansas and Oklahoma in good to excellent condition.</p>
<p>But in Texas, where some areas were still in need of moisture, only 58 percent of the crop was rated in good to excellent condition.  </p>
